#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to build a C extension for your Qiskit workflow in Python"
msgstr "Paano gumawa ng C extension para sa iyong Qiskit workflow sa Python"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extend Qiskit in Python with C"
msgstr "Palawakin ang Qiskit sa Python gamit ang C"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore strcmp */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore strcmp */}\n"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extend Qiskit in Python with C {#extend-qiskit-in-python-with-c}"
msgstr "Palawakin ang Qiskit sa Python gamit ang C {#extend-qiskit-in-python-with-c}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit C API can be used within Python extension modules.\n"
"You can write performance-critical sections of your Qiskit extensions in C to accelerate them, and\n"
"then safely distribute these to your users.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Qiskit C API ay maaaring gamitin sa loob ng mga Python extension module.\n"
"Maaari kang sumulat ng mga performance-critical na seksyon ng iyong mga Qiskit extension sa C para mapabilis ang mga ito, at\n"
"pagkatapos ay ligtas na ipamahagi ang mga ito sa iyong mga gumagamit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide walks you through the process of defining a complete extension module, configuring\n"
"its build process, and exposing it to Python users.  The package provides a simple port of\n"
"[`AddSpectatorMeasures` from the Qiskit addons][AddSpectatorMeasures-code] to C.  This is a real custom\n"
"pass with a real use case in the Qiskit addons.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagabayan ka ng gabay na ito sa proseso ng pagtatakda ng isang kumpletong extension module, pag-configure ng\n"
"proseso ng pagbuo nito, at pag-expose nito sa mga gumagamit ng Python. Nagbibigay ang package ng isang simpleng port ng\n"
"[`AddSpectatorMeasures` mula sa Qiskit addons][AddSpectatorMeasures-code] sa C. Ito ay isang tunay na custom\n"
"pass na may tunay na kaso ng paggamit sa Qiskit addons.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid "[AddSpectatorMeasures-code]: https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-utils/blob/e0582e4aa856dc7b152bacbe0c20d1fa306d9640/qiskit_addon_utils/noise_management/post_selection/transpiler/passes/add_spectator_measures.py#L32-L157"
msgstr "[AddSpectatorMeasures-code]: https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-addon-utils/blob/e0582e4aa856dc7b152bacbe0c20d1fa306d9640/qiskit_addon_utils/noise_management/post_selection/transpiler/passes/add_spectator_measures.py#L32-L157"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"  You might find the following external resources helpful:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"  Maaaring makapagtulong ang mga sumusunod na panlabas na mapagkukunan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[The CPython documentation on writing extension modules](https://docs.python.org/3/extending/index.html).\n"
msgstr "[Ang dokumentasyon ng CPython sa pagsulat ng mga extension module](https://docs.python.org/3/extending/index.html).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[The NumPy documentation on using its C API](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/user/c-info.how-to-extend.html).\n"
msgstr "[Ang dokumentasyon ng NumPy sa paggamit ng C API nito](https://numpy.org/doc/stable/user/c-info.how-to-extend.html).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The Qiskit C API is exposed for Python extension modules in a very similar manner to the NumPy C\n"
"  API.  If you have previously programmed a NumPy extension, you will find the Qiskit process\n"
"  familiar.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ang Qiskit C API ay ini-expose para sa mga Python extension module sa paraang katulad ng NumPy C\n"
"  API. Kung nakapag-program ka na ng NumPy extension dati, makikita mong pamilyar ang proseso ng Qiskit.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"  The Qiskit C API is still experimental. Thus, there is not yet a fully stable programming or\n"
"  binary interface, and there might be breaking changes between minor versions.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"warning\">\n"
"  Ang Qiskit C API ay eksperimental pa rin. Kaya naman, wala pa nitong ganap na matatag na programming o\n"
"  binary interface, at maaaring magkaroon ng mga breaking change sa pagitan ng mga minor na bersyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  For example, an extension module using Qiskit v2.4.0 at build time is guaranteed to work with\n"
"  Qiskit v2.4.1 at runtime, but might break when using Qiskit v2.5.0 at runtime.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Halimbawa, ang isang extension module na gumagamit ng Qiskit v2.4.0 sa oras ng pagbuo ay garantisadong gagana sa\n"
"  Qiskit v2.4.1 sa oras ng runtime, ngunit maaaring masira kapag gumagamit ng Qiskit v2.5.0 sa oras ng runtime.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements {#requirements}"
msgstr "Mga Kinakailangan {#requirements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complete the instructions in the [Install](/guides/install-c-api) topic to install the following:\n"
msgstr "Tapusin ang mga tagubilin sa paksang [Install](/guides/install-c-api) para i-install ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The standard C compiler toolchain for your platform\n"
msgstr "Ang standard na C compiler toolchain para sa iyong platform\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A version of Python that includes its C API headers. \n"
msgstr "Isang bersyon ng Python na may kasamang mga C API header nito. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You should also be familiar with, or prepared to look up, the functions and objects available\n"
"in the [Qiskit C API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-c), and should have some familiarity with C programming.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dapat ka ring pamilyar sa, o handa na hanapin, ang mga function at object na available\n"
"sa [Qiskit C API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-c), at dapat kang may kaunting kaalaman sa C programming.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start from a clean directory.\n"
msgstr "Magsimula mula sa isang malinis na direktoryo.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid "[c-api]: /docs/api/qiskit-c"
msgstr "[c-api]: /docs/api/qiskit-c"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the directory structure {#create-the-directory-structure}"
msgstr "Gumawa ng istruktura ng direktoryo {#create-the-directory-structure}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use a `src`-based directory structure and a simple `setuptools`-based build system.  These\n"
"instructions should be easy adapt to any build system that can build\n"
"extension modules.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamit tayo ng `src`-based na istruktura ng direktoryo at isang simpleng `setuptools`-based na build system. Ang mga\n"
"instruksyong ito ay dapat madaling iaangkop sa anumang build system na makakapagtayo ng\n"
"mga extension module.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final structure will look like:\n"
msgstr "Ang panghuling istruktura ay magiging ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In summary:\n"
msgstr "Sa buod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pyproject.toml` defines the standard static metadata about the Python package we are creating,\n"
"including its name, author, and build- and run-time dependencies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng `pyproject.toml` ang karaniwang static na metadata tungkol sa Python package na ginagawa natin,\n"
"kasama ang pangalan, may-akda, at mga dependency sa oras ng pagbuo at runtime.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`setup.py` contains the minimal dynamic configuration we need to build our extension module.\n"
msgstr "Naglalaman ang `setup.py` ng minimal na dynamic na configuration na kailangan natin para itayo ang ating extension module.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`src/spectator_measures/__init__.py` defines the user-facing interface and provides some code to\n"
"interface with Qiskit's Python-space components.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng `src/spectator_measures/__init__.py` ang interface na nakaharap sa gumagamit at nagbibigay ng ilang code para\n"
"makipag-ugnayan sa mga component ng Qiskit sa Python-space.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c` defines the C extension module, which will contain all the\n"
"performance-critical code of our package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng `src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c` ang C extension module, na maglalaman ng lahat ng\n"
"performance-critical na code ng ating package.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will examine each file in detail, building up the package with its extension module.\n"
msgstr "Susuriin natin ang bawat file nang detalyado, binubuo ang package kasama ang extension module nito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the package metadata {#define-the-package-metadata}"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang metadata ng package {#define-the-package-metadata}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Begin by defining the `pyproject.toml` file. This is standard for a `setuptools`-based\n"
"project, although  `qiskit` is an additional requirement in the `build-system.requires` array,\n"
"in addition to `setuptools`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula sa pamamagitan ng pagtukoy sa file na `pyproject.toml`. Ito ay standard para sa isang `setuptools`-based\n"
"na proyekto, bagaman ang `qiskit` ay isang karagdagang kinakailangan sa array na `build-system.requires`,\n"
"bilang karagdagan sa `setuptools`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`pyproject.toml`**\n"
msgstr "**`pyproject.toml`**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Set Qiskit's runtime version in\n"
"`project.dependencies` to match the minor version used at build time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Itakda ang runtime version ng Qiskit sa\n"
"`project.dependencies` para tumugma sa minor version na ginamit sa oras ng build.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In many pure-Python `setuptools`-based projects, it would be sufficient to have the\n"
"`pyproject.toml` file.  However, our module needs access to the Qiskit C API header files during\n"
"its build process.   Starting with v2.4, these are included in the Qiskit SDK Python distributions.\n"
"To locate the directory containing them, run `qiskit.capi.get_include()`.\n"
"This results in a `setup.py` file that looks like:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa maraming purong Python na `setuptools`-based na proyekto, sapat na ang magkaroon ng\n"
"`pyproject.toml` file. Gayunpaman, ang aming module ay nangangailangan ng access sa mga Qiskit C API header file sa panahon ng\n"
"proseso ng pagbuo nito. Simula sa v2.4, kasama na ang mga ito sa mga Python distribution ng Qiskit SDK.\n"
"Para mahanap ang direktoryo na naglalaman ng mga ito, patakbuhin ang `qiskit.capi.get_include()`.\n"
"Nagreresulta ito sa isang `setup.py` file na ganito ang hitsura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`setup.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`setup.py`**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most of the package information is defined in `pyproject.toml`, and `setuptools.setup()` will\n"
"also read that file.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karamihan ng impormasyon ng package ay tinukoy sa `pyproject.toml`, at ang `setuptools.setup()` ay\n"
"magbabasa rin ng file na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"See the [`setuptools` User Guide](https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/latest/userguide/) for more\n"
"information on configuring `setuptools`-based projects.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"Tingnan ang [`setuptools` User Guide](https://setuptools.pypa.io/en/latest/userguide/) para sa karagdagang\n"
"impormasyon sa pag-configure ng mga `setuptools`-based na proyekto.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the Python-space wrapper {#write-the-python-space-wrapper}"
msgstr "Isulat ang Python-space wrapper {#write-the-python-space-wrapper}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is technically possible to define everything in a Python extension from C.  In practice, it is\n"
"easier to interact with other Python-space code from Python itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Teknikal na posibleng tukuyin ang lahat sa isang Python extension mula sa C. Sa pagsasagawa, mas\n"
"madaling makipag-ugnayan sa ibang Python-space code mula sa Python mismo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This package defines a custom transpiler pass that derives from the Python-space\n"
"`qiskit.transpiler.TransformationPass` class, but uses a function from the C extension module for\n"
"all of its business logic.  This looks like:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng package na ito ang isang custom transpiler pass na nagmumula sa Python-space\n"
"`qiskit.transpiler.TransformationPass` class, ngunit gumagamit ng function mula sa C extension module para sa\n"
"lahat ng business logic nito. Ganito ang hitsura nito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`src/spectator_measures/__init__.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`src/spectator_measures/__init__.py`**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The exact details of this pass are unimportant for this guide.  If you are interested, you can\n"
"consult the [`AddSpectatorMeasures` API documentation in\n"
"`qiskit-addon-utils`][AddSpectatorMeasures-api].  This guide produces a simple port of that pass,\n"
"without support for control-flow operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang eksaktong mga detalye ng pass na ito ay hindi mahalaga para sa gabay na ito. Kung interesado ka, maaari mong\n"
"tingnan ang [`AddSpectatorMeasures` API documentation sa\n"
"`qiskit-addon-utils`][AddSpectatorMeasures-api]. Gumagawa ang gabay na ito ng isang simpleng port ng pass na iyon,\n"
"nang walang suporta para sa mga operasyon ng control-flow.\n"

#. type: Link reference
#, no-wrap
msgid "[AddSpectatorMeasures-api]: https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.noise_management.post_selection.transpiler.passes.AddSpectatorMeasures.html"
msgstr "[AddSpectatorMeasures-api]: https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-utils/stubs/qiskit_addon_utils.noise_management.post_selection.transpiler.passes.AddSpectatorMeasures.html"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the C extension module {#write-the-c-extension-module}"
msgstr "Isulat ang C extension module {#write-the-c-extension-module}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"  You may find the following resources helpful:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\">\n"
"  Maaaring makapagtulong ang mga sumusunod na mapagkukunan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  - [The Qiskit C API reference][c-api].\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  - [Ang Qiskit C API reference][c-api].\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section is concerned with the actual C extension.  This is the most complex file in the\n"
"project, so we will split it into stages.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang seksyong ito ay tungkol sa aktwal na C extension. Ito ang pinaka-kumplikadong file sa\n"
"proyekto, kaya hahati-hatiin natin ito sa mga yugto.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure the header files {#configure-the-header-files}"
msgstr "I-configure ang mga header file {#configure-the-header-files}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When building a Python extension module, you must include `Python.h` before any other file.\n"
"To use the Qiskit C API in an extension module, you must define the macro\n"
"`QISKIT_PYTHON_EXTENSION` before including `qiskit.h`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nagtatayo ng Python extension module, kailangan mong isama ang `Python.h` bago ang anumang ibang file.\n"
"Para gamitin ang Qiskit C API sa isang extension module, kailangan mong tukuyin ang macro na\n"
"`QISKIT_PYTHON_EXTENSION` bago isama ang `qiskit.h`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our includes then look like:\n"
msgstr "Ang aming mga include ay magiging ganito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c`**\n"
msgstr "**`src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c`**\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the pure C API code {#write-the-pure-c-api-code}"
msgstr "Isulat ang purong C API code {#write-the-pure-c-api-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, write all of the business logic as pure Qiskit C API code.  We will expose\n"
"this logic to Python space in the following section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, isulat ang lahat ng business logic bilang purong Qiskit C API code. Ie-expose natin\n"
"ang logic na ito sa Python space sa sumusunod na seksyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section contains only pure Qiskit C API code.  It uses the C API types:\n"
msgstr "Ang seksyong ito ay naglalaman lamang ng purong Qiskit C API code. Gumagamit ito ng mga uri ng C API:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QkDag *`, corresponding to the Python-space `DAGCircuit`.\n"
msgstr "`QkDag *`, na tumutugma sa Python-space `DAGCircuit`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QkTarget *`, corresponding to the Python-space `Target`.\n"
msgstr "`QkTarget *`, na tumutugma sa Python-space `Target`.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QkNeighbors`, a native C API type representing two-qubit coupling constraints.\n"
msgstr "`QkNeighbors`, isang native C API type na kumakatawan sa mga two-qubit coupling constraint.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`QkCircuitInstruction`, a native C API type for querying individual instructions.\n"
msgstr "`QkCircuitInstruction`, isang native C API type para sa pag-query ng mga indibidwal na instruksyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first two form part of our interaction with Python space, but when working with them, we\n"
"only need to consider the pure C API.  There is no interaction with the Python\n"
"interpreter in this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang dalawa ay bumubuo ng aming pakikipag-ugnayan sa Python space, ngunit kapag nagtatrabaho sa mga ito, kailangan nating\n"
"isaalang-alang lamang ang purong C API. Walang pakikipag-ugnayan sa Python\n"
"interpreter sa code na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that all functions and symbols defined in this section are declared with `static` linkage.\n"
"This is because the Python interpreter will not link against this extension module; we will provide\n"
"the interpreter with details of the available functions in the next section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang lahat ng function at symbol na tinukoy sa seksyong ito ay idineklara gamit ang `static` linkage.\n"
"Ito ay dahil ang Python interpreter ay hindi mag-li-link laban sa extension module na ito; ibibigay natin\n"
"sa interpreter ang mga detalye ng mga available na function sa susunod na seksyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not dwell on the algorithmic details of this code; it is instructive to use a meaningful\n"
"transpiler pass for the demonstration, but the precise implementation of the algorithm is not\n"
"important to this guide.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi na tayo magtatagal sa mga detalye ng algorithm ng code na ito; kapaki-pakinabang na gumamit ng makabuluhang\n"
"transpiler pass para sa demonstrasyon, ngunit ang tiyak na pagpapatupad ng algorithm ay hindi\n"
"mahalaga sa gabay na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c (appended)`**\n"
msgstr "**`src/spectator_measures/_coremodule.c (appended)`**\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the Python interaction code {#write-the-python-interaction-code}"
msgstr "Isulat ang Python interaction code {#write-the-python-interaction-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of the business logic is now defined in pure C.  Next, it needs to be safely exposed to Python.\n"
msgstr "Ang lahat ng business logic ay natukoy na ngayon sa purong C. Susunod, kailangan itong ligtas na i-expose sa Python.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To begin, define the only function that will be exposed to Python.  This must\n"
"follow a defined signature, which is purely in terms of Python types that look like a\n"
"`fn(self, *args, **kwargs)` method.  We have to return a `PyObject *`, which is the generic form of\n"
"any Python object.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para magsimula, tukuyin ang tanging function na ie-expose sa Python. Dapat itong\n"
"sumunod sa isang tinukoy na signature, na purong nasa mga uri ng Python na mukhang isang\n"
"`fn(self, *args, **kwargs)` na method. Kailangan nating magbalik ng `PyObject *`, na siyang generic na anyo ng\n"
"anumang Python object.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The complete function looks like:\n"
msgstr "Ang kumpletong function ay ganito ang hitsura:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In brief, the function:\n"
msgstr "Sa maikling salita, ang function ay:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Follows a defined signature to accept arbitrary Python arguments.\n"
msgstr "Sumusunod sa isang tinukoy na signature para tanggapin ang mga arbitrary na Python argument.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Defines space to store C-native objects parsed out of the Python arguments.\n"
msgstr "Nagtatukoy ng espasyo para iimbak ang mga C-native object na na-parse mula sa mga Python argument.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Calls a parsing function to extract the C-native objects, configured with the list of expected\n"
"arguments, keyword arguments, and the functions to use to convert them.  If this fails, the\n"
"function propagates the error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tumatawag ng parsing function para kunin ang mga C-native object, na naka-configure gamit ang listahan ng mga inaasahang\n"
"argument, keyword argument, at mga function na gagamitin para ma-convert ang mga ito. Kung nabigo ito, ang\n"
"function ay nagpapalaganap ng error.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delegates to the C-native business logic of the previous section, which mutates the DAG in place.\n"
msgstr "Ini-delegate sa C-native na business logic ng nakaraang seksyon, na nagbabago ng DAG sa lugar.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Returns the Python-space `None` object.\n"
msgstr "Nagbabalik ng Python-space `None` object.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most complex logic is all inside `PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords`.  This is well documented in [the\n"
"CPython documentation on parsing arguments](https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/arg.html), which you\n"
"should consult for further information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pinaka-kumplikadong logic ay nasa loob ng `PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords`. Ito ay mahusay na dokumentado sa [the\n"
"CPython documentation on parsing arguments](https://docs.python.org/3/c-api/arg.html), na dapat mong\n"
"tingnan para sa karagdagang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit C API provides several functions with names like `qk_*_convert_from_python`, which are\n"
"designed as \"converter\" functions for use with `PyArg_Parse*`functions.  These correspond to the\n"
"`O&` keys in the format string; here, we used `qk_dag_convert_from_python` and\n"
"`qk_target_convert_from_python`.  These functions _borrow_ the C-native object from the Python\n"
"argument they are derived from.  This means that mutations will propagate to Python space, but also that\n"
"you should take care not to release your reference to the Python object that backs them, while using\n"
"the result.  This is standard for Python C API programming.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Qiskit C API ay nagbibigay ng ilang function na may mga pangalan tulad ng `qk_*_convert_from_python`, na dinisenyo\n"
"bilang mga \"converter\" function para gamitin sa `PyArg_Parse*` na mga function. Ang mga ito ay tumutugma sa\n"
"mga `O&` key sa format string; dito, gumamit tayo ng `qk_dag_convert_from_python` at\n"
"`qk_target_convert_from_python`. Ang mga function na ito ay _nangongoha_ ng C-native object mula sa Python\n"
"argument na pinagmulan nito. Ibig sabihin, ang mga pagbabago ay magpapalaganap sa Python space, ngunit pati na rin na\n"
"dapat kang mag-ingat na huwag palayain ang iyong reference sa Python object na nagsasuporth sa kanila, habang ginagamit\n"
"ang resulta. Ito ay standard para sa Python C API programming.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we define the information about this module and the function it contains, so we can pass it to\n"
"Python space:\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tinutukoy natin ang impormasyon tungkol sa module na ito at ang function na naglalaman nito, para maipasa natin ito sa\n"
"Python space:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This method table and module-definition structure are described in more detail in [the CPython\n"
"documentation on module\n"
"initialization](https://docs.python.org/3/extending/extending.html#the-module-s-method-table-and-initialization-function).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang method table at module-definition structure na ito ay inilarawan nang mas detalyado sa [the CPython\n"
"documentation on module\n"
"initialization](https://docs.python.org/3/extending/extending.html#the-module-s-method-table-and-initialization-function).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, tell Python how to initialize the module.  This is the only function in the C\n"
"file that is exported.  Its name _must_ exactly match the pattern\n"
"`PyInit_<mod>`, where `<mod>` is the (unqualified) module name.  In this case, the fully\n"
"qualified module name is `spectator_measures._core`, and the unqualified name is `_core`, so our\n"
"function must be called `PyInit__core`, with the double underscore.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, sabihin sa Python kung paano i-initialize ang module. Ito ang tanging function sa C\n"
"file na ine-export. Ang pangalan nito ay _dapat_ na eksaktong tumugma sa pattern na\n"
"`PyInit_<mod>`, kung saan ang `<mod>` ay ang (unqualified) na pangalan ng module. Sa kasong ito, ang fully\n"
"qualified na pangalan ng module ay `spectator_measures._core`, at ang unqualified na pangalan ay `_core`, kaya ang aming\n"
"function ay dapat tawaging `PyInit__core`, na may double underscore.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `PyMODINIT_FUNC` and `PyModuleDef_Init` symbols are both standard Python C API programming.  The\n"
"Qiskit-specific component is `qk_import()`.  It is critical that you call this function during the\n"
"initialization function of your module; you will not be able to call any Qiskit C API functions\n"
"until this has been successfully executed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang `PyMODINIT_FUNC` at `PyModuleDef_Init` na mga symbol ay parehong standard Python C API programming. Ang\n"
"Qiskit-specific na component ay `qk_import()`. Kritikal na tawagin mo ang function na ito sa panahon ng initialization\n"
"function ng iyong module; hindi ka makakatawag ng anumang Qiskit C API function\n"
"hanggang sa matagumpay na mapatupad ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the package from Python {#use-the-package-from-python}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang package mula sa Python {#use-the-package-from-python}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is now a complete package, including a C extension module.  Because only standard\n"
"tooling was used, and no non-standard system libraries are linked during build time,\n"
"the build process is simple.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay isang kumpletong package na ngayon, kasama ang isang C extension module. Dahil standard lamang ang\n"
"mga tooling na ginamit, at walang non-standard na system library na naka-link sa oras ng pagbuo,\n"
"ang proseso ng pagbuo ay simple.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use any PEP-517-compatible build tool.  As a minimal example, you can run the following command in the repository root to install the package.\n"
msgstr "Maaari kang gumamit ng anumang PEP-517-compatible na build tool. Bilang minimal na halimbawa, maaari mong patakbuhin ang sumusunod na command sa repository root para i-install ang package.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This compiles the C extension module and\n"
"installs the complete Python package in your environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kino-compile nito ang C extension module at\n"
"ini-install ang kumpletong Python package sa iyong environment.\n"

